WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.458
Welcome to Tokyo.

00:00:02.583 --> 00:00:06.333
This city has an endless list of things
to see and experience.

00:00:06.833 --> 00:00:09.416
It can all be a bit overwhelming to
know where to even begin.

00:00:09.958 --> 00:00:13.083
I've been lucky enough to explore
this city on multiple trips,

00:00:13.416 --> 00:00:15.541
and I'll be sharing it all in this video.

00:00:15.958 --> 00:00:17.916
From iconic sites to hidden gems,

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:20.250
from street food to sushi bars,

00:00:20.791 --> 00:00:24.125
this guide is here to help you plan
the perfect Tokyo adventure.

00:00:25.541 --> 00:00:27.666
If you're ready, then let's dive into one

00:00:27.666 --> 00:00:29.958
of the most exciting cities
on this planet.

00:00:33.375 --> 00:00:35.791
First things first, how to
get around the city.

00:00:36.875 --> 00:00:40.333
Tokyo has one of the most efficient public
transport systems in the world,

00:00:40.708 --> 00:00:42.416
and we're going to take full
advantage of it.

00:00:42.791 --> 00:00:44.958
The best way to get around
is with an IC Card,

00:00:45.333 --> 00:00:47.416
a rechargeable travel card you can use on

00:00:47.416 --> 00:00:49.708
pretty much all trains,
subways and buses.

00:00:50.208 --> 00:00:54.000
You can get a physical one or go digital
like I did and add it to your phone.

00:00:54.875 --> 00:00:57.916
Just top it up through Apple Pay or
at stations around the city.

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:01.291
Super convenient and you can easily
track your spending as you go.

00:01:02.416 --> 00:01:04.875
For navigation, Google Maps
is your best friend.

00:01:05.333 --> 00:01:07.083
It works great in Japan and gives you

00:01:07.083 --> 00:01:10.458
step-by-step directions, train
routes and transit times.

00:01:11.083 --> 00:01:13.458
If you're exploring on your
own, it's a must-have.

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:16.958
For language help, Google Translate
comes in clutch.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:20.583
Just point your camera at signs or
menus to have them translated

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.000
or use it when communicating with locals.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:26.333
But for all this to work, you will
need data on your phone.

